  "representation": {
    "realm": "Default slice backing, transfer and immutable slicing derive the intrinsic prototype from the native method execution realm. Borrowed methods keep that realm; explicit species construction remains observable and retains its constructor realm. Global constructor replacement cannot replace the intrinsic owner.",
    "index": "Ordinary and immutable slicing share array_buffer_slice_index for ToNumber, truncation and clamping. Removed the duplicate closure, which incorrectly mapped negative zero to the buffer end.",
    "species": "Sharedness validation uses result_shared != receiver_shared, rejecting both ArrayBuffer-to-SharedArrayBuffer and reverse species substitution. No new flags, side maps, production JS shims or benchmark/fixture identities."
  },
  "specs": [
    "https://tc39.es/ecma262/multipage/structured-data.html#sec-arraybuffer.prototype.slice",
